// stage1-only
// extern declares a function the linker must resolve; the compiler emits no
// code for it. Declaring without calling compiles in every mode - only a
// call without -c and the linker is an error (extern.qela).
extern fn qela_link_fail(a i64) i64;
fn main() int {
	return 42;
}
